        "content": "In 2022-Q2, development shifted from the previous quarter’s fix-heavy work to feature-driven enhancements, with 30 commits and 13 PRs across 9 active repositories, led by the Simple-XX/SimpleKernel project. Technical efforts concentrated on RISC-V CPU support, interrupt handling, and virtual memory management, introducing structures like `satp`, `pte_t`, `sstatus_t`, and PLIC constants while systematically applying `constexpr` and internal clean-ups. A new documentation series (doc/01 through doc/8) was added, reflecting a broader focus beyond core kernel code. Collaboration patterns evolved from solo work to include one code review with a merge approval comment, and issue tracking began with 2 issues and 5 comments, indicating an emerging review culture. Compared to Q1’s single-repo, fix-dominated activity with 119 commits and 0 reviews, this quarter saw a deliberate shift toward feature delivery, multi-repo involvement, and initial peer review, trading raw commit volume for a more structured and collaborative approach.",
